blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:97:	Definition~\ref{def:projective-strategy-general} is the general notion: a strategy for an arbitrary nonlocal game all of whose measurements are projective. The low individual degree chapters use the same term for the concrete data of a two-prover strategy for the $(m,q,d)$ low individual degree test (Definition~\ref{def:projective-strategy} in Chapter~\ref{chap:test}); that definition is the specialization of the present notion to the question format of that particular test. The two usages occur in disjoint contexts.
